Certainly! Below is the modified sequence of client requests with the `CWD` (Change Working Directory) and `STAT` (Status) commands added in appropriate locations:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
CWD /path/to/directory  ; (Add the appropriate path you want to change to)
STAT
LIST
MKD test
QUIT
```

In this sequence, the `CWD` command is placed after the `PORT` command to set the working directory before listing the files and creating a new directory. The `STAT` command is placed right after the `CWD` command to check the status of the current working directory. 

Make sure to replace `/path/to/directory` with the actual directory path you want to change into

